# What the examples of `acme` stand on: the test server the environment
# names, its authority, the challenge server it resolves names through, and
# a certificate request recorded once. With no `ACME_DIRECTORY`, every
# example that needs a server says it skipped.
#
# The variables: `ACME_DIRECTORY`, the directory's URL, as
# "https://localhost:14000/dir" for Pebble; `ACME_ROOTS`, the path of the
# PEM of the authority its TLS certificate is signed by, Pebble's
# `pebble.minica.pem`; `ACME_CHALLTEST`, the management URL of Pebble's
# challenge server, "http://127.0.0.1:8055" where unset.

use bytes
use http
use json
use os

# The name the recorded request is for.
constant CSR_NAME: str
    "example.heroes-test.example"

# A certificate request for `CSR_NAME`, its DER, made by OpenSSL 3 on
# 2026-11-19 with a P-256 key thrown away after (`openssl req -new -newkey
# ec`, its self-signature verified by `openssl req -verify`).
